# alone, and the current tree no longer contains it (common/t/setuptoken.t
# assembles the value at runtime instead). This line retires the
# historical hit only.
#
# Two entries, two attempts: the first tried splitting the literal into
# fragments, which did NOT help -- the rule fires on the entropy of
# whatever token follows the word "secret", and one fragment was still
# over the threshold. The tests now DERIVE their signing values from a
# repeated string, so there is no literal left to flag.
